  "verbalization": "The compound (1R,2S,4R,10S,11R,13S,16S)-11-hydroxy-11-methyl-4-prop-1-en-2-yl-14-oxatetracyclo[8.5.1.02,8.013,16]hexadec-7-ene-6,9,15-trione is associated with the CD276 antigen through multiple pathways. It is a target of two different compounds, Ajugaciliatin E and Flavipin, both of which are linked to the CD276 antigen. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of CD276, potentially through enzymatic activity, as it is targeted by dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family members. The consistent association across three distinct paths, with similar scores, indicates a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role of the compound in regulating CD276, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the nature of this interaction."
